    title: "Black Feminisms",
    units: 0.5,
    description: "Through the sustained and in-depth study of foundational Black feminist organizers, activists, artists, theorists, and public figures, this course will analyze the interconnected themes of race and gender. Students will examine the meaningful ways that Black women have shaped feminist studies, gender studies, art, popular culture, civic, and social movements.",
